WEBVTT

00:13:56.660 --> 00:14:00.266
What's your version of hanging out
with kids at recess?

00:14:00.290 --> 00:14:03.388
For an architect, it might be strolling
by a building you designed

00:14:03.412 --> 00:14:06.046
to see how people are living
or working in it.

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:09.787
For a business manager, it could be
an individual check-in with a team member

00:14:09.811 --> 00:14:13.206
to ask how they're doing
and how you can help them.

00:14:13.230 --> 00:14:15.469
For me, it's carving out
a little time each week

00:14:15.493 --> 00:14:17.736
to send notes
of appreciation to colleagues

00:14:17.760 --> 00:14:19.683
and recommend students for jobs.

00:14:19.707 --> 00:14:20.715
(Music)

00:14:20.739 --> 00:14:23.666
Small wins aren't hard to find
if you look for them.

00:14:23.690 --> 00:14:26.746
But as Anne Helen Petersen
knows all too well,

00:14:26.770 --> 00:14:28.723
sometimes you land in a situation at work

00:14:28.747 --> 00:14:31.025
where it feels
like you're just on a treadmill.